    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (73.77) and **Yordan Alvarez** (72.97) anchor the Zurich Zebras as our most potent offensive weapons. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from an elite setup against Gausman, buoyed by a prime leadoff spot and a high stolen base probability due to a slow opposing delivery. **Yordan Alvarez** remains our premier UTIL play, leveraging an elite .450 xwOBA to overcome a neutral park factor against Bibee. Additionally, **Junior Caminero** (67.50) registers as a top-tier start; while his raw base is tempered by park factors, he holds a significant platoon edge against a weak 5.00 xERA arm in Poulin, cementing his status as a must-start in the cleanup spot.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved our bench, where **Luke Raley** (38.57) fell just short of a starting berth. Despite the optimizer looking for potential utility value, **Luke Raley** was squeezed out due to a difficult same-handed matchup against Ranger Suarez and an inherent risk associated with a \"Lineup Pending\" designation. Elsewhere, **Dillon Dingler** (57.50) continues to be an intriguing play; his score is significantly propped up by a dynamic platoon advantage against Eisert and favorable wind conditions that reward his recent high-contact output. \n\nWe must remain cautious of the lower-floor plays currently in the lineup, specifically **Colt Keith** (42.00) and **Caleb Durbin** (43.63), who are battling both regression and unfavorable platoon splits. While **Caleb Durbin** provides necessary category coverage, his inclusion remains volatile pending official confirmation of his position in the order. We are keeping **Christian Yelich** (59.62) active despite a slight disadvantageous platoon against P\u00e9rez, as his leadoff duties and professional pedigree provide a necessary floor for the team's total output. All eyes remain on the bench to ensure **Trea Turner**, **Hyeseong Kim**, **Rece Hinds**, **Kyle Schwarber**, **Carson Benge**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Zac Veen**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Josh Smith**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, **Jose Fernandez**, and **Pedro Ramirez** are prepared should injury reports shift our strategy mid-day.",
